    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora collects content source files from directories in branches, tags, and worktrees of git repositories. These source files are only retrieved and processed correctly if Antora can locate them within a content source root."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The source files containing a site’s content are stored in one or more git repositories. These repositories can be remote, local, or a combination of both. In a playbook file, you’ll enter several parameters (e.g., url, branches, tags, and start paths) that:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "olist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "allow Antora to locate and connect to your content source repositories, and"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "provide Antora with the location criteria that resolves to one or more "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "content source roots"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "#content-source-root"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " within a git repository."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": "arabic",
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the repository is local, by default Antora will attempt to use the worktree of that repository if the current branch matches one of the branches defined on the content source. This behavior is configurable."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora requires a local directory to be a git repository, which means the local directory is a git worktree. The git repository itself can be empty, meaning you don’t have to commit any files in order for it to work. If the local directory is not yet a git repository, you can make it one by running the following commands:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ git init . && git commit --allow-empty -m init"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora recognizes any submodule of a locally-cloned repository as a discrete content respository. That means that the content source URL can point to the submodule directory and Antora will treat that folder as a git repository, with its own branches, tags, and start paths."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora does not support submodules in a remote (managed) repositories since the git client Antora uses doesn’t recursively clone submodules."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "warning"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Before configuring a site’s playbook, you’ll want to determine where to set up the content source roots in your repositories."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "git-and-content-sources",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "git repositories and content sources"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "content source root"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a location in a branch or tag (i.e., a reference) of a repository from where Antora begins looking for content source files. Think of the content source root as the entrance of the store where Antora shops. From the content source root, Antora looks for an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "antora.yml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " file, which identifies the component version bucket, then scans for a collection of source files organized in a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "standard set of directories"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "standard-directories.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to add to that bucket."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A repository can have many content source roots. You may have one content source root per branch or tag. Or you may have multiple content source roots per branch or tag defined using "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "multiple start paths"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "playbook:content-source-start-paths.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". You can also have a combination of both. Where you store the content source roots is up to you."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "content-source-root",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "What’s a content source root?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Repositories and Content Source Roots"
      }
    ]
  }
}
